Comment: Modified in September 2026 and built from GNOME Network Displays
 0.99.0. The modifications are the thirty-one patches installed alongside this file,
 covering encoder selection, stream unit naming, shutdown, PulseAudio teardown,
 a use-after-free in receiver discovery, reuse of the screen sharing
 permission, choosing the streamed display mode from both ends of the link,
 building without GTK, running streams inside a Flatpak sandbox, a
 configurable D-Bus name prefix, keeping the screen sharing permission
 inside a Flatpak sandbox, publishing each stream's state on D-Bus,
 reporting a stream the user ended from the desktop, finding the stream
 helper beside the daemon, sending the desktop's sound to the receiver,
 capturing that sound in larger periods, a shorter pipeline latency with
 x264, scaling, converting and encoding video in parallel, dropping frames
 only when they would be late, a higher video bitrate limit, sending sooner
 with x264, counting dropped frames correctly, respecting the receiver's
 slice limit, using the constrained high profile when it gives a better
 mode, two fixes to the CEA mode table, holding x264 under its bitrate
 limit, sending frames evenly, keeping the PCR on video, letting the client
 pause discovery, retrying a failed mDNS resolve, and sending every bit of
 the chosen mode. The complete upstream source archive is installed at
 /usr/share/doc/mirdispo/gnome-network-displays-0.99.0.tar.xz;
 applying the patches to it in numerical order reproduces the source these
 binaries were built from.

